  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Israel condemns Green party passing ‘Zionism is racism’ as a ‘stain on history of UK’ – UK politics live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/oct/04/conservatives-tories-conference-kemi-badenoch-james-cleverly-labour-jury-trials-green-party-zionism-uk-politics-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>Party formally adopts policy which equates Zionism with racism, as all <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/04/green-party-votes-adopt-policy-zionism-racism\">Green party votes to adopt policy that equates Zionism with racism</a></p><p></p><p>On Friday the Times <a href=\"https://www.thetimes.com/uk/politics/article/katie-lam-pension-triple-lock-conservatives-vkxdz9thb\">revealed</a> that <strong>Katie Lam</strong>, the communities secretary, told a meeting in private earlier this year that the state pension system needs a fundamental overhaul.</p><p>Speaking in June, when she was a frontbencher but not yet in the shadow cabinet, Lam was asked at a meeting with activists if she thought the pensions triple lock was sustainable. She replied:</p><p>Ultimately I think what we will need in the end is an entirely new pension system.</p><p>I mean, a baby that is born today has a 20% chance of living to be 100 and I don’t think we can fund one in five people half of their lives, you know, for the first 20 and the last 30 years. But obviously if you are 90 you probably can’t go out and get a job right, so I think you have to be realistic about how you would taper that and bring that in across the population.</p><p>The fact is, the triple lock and pensions are things that people have contributed to.</p><p>Conservatives believe that if you have contributed, then you deserve to get your state pension.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/oct/04/conservatives-tories-conference-kemi-badenoch-james-cleverly-labour-jury-trials-green-party-zionism-uk-politics-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-04T15:51:31"
    },
    {
      "title": "Green party votes to adopt policy that equates Zionism with racism",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/04/green-party-votes-adopt-policy-zionism-racism",
      "description": "<p>Motion calling for single Palestinian state, which is opposed by most Green MPs and expected to be challenged, passes by 1,022 votes to 813</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/oct/04/conservatives-tories-conference-kemi-badenoch-james-cleverly-labour-jury-trials-green-party-zionism-uk-politics-latest-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>The Greens in England and Wales have formally adopted a policy that equates Zionism with racism and calls for Israel to be replaced by a single Palestinian state.</p><p>The move is expected to be challenged by some party members under equality laws, with one leading KC saying such a case would have a good chance of succeeding.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/04/green-party-votes-adopt-policy-zionism-racism\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-04T15:43:41"
    }
  ]
